  "declared_proposition": "For 0<r<1 and m>=1, the normalized Abel Omega projector Q_r(m)=r^(-1) sum_{j=1}^m (-1)^(j-1) j binom(m,j) r^j equals m(1-r)^(m-1). Thus Q_r(1)=1 but Q_r(m)>0 for every composite multiplicity m>=2, so no fixed r is an exact prime indicator. For each integer X>=1, however, r_X=1-1/(16X) gives an exact finite identity: if S_X=sum_{X<n<=2X} Q_rX(Omega(n))Q_rX(Omega(n+2)) and T_X is the number of twin-prime lower endpoints in that interval, then T_X<=S_X<=T_X+1/8, hence floor(S_X)=T_X.",
